IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nt-sa`
IMPORT `nt-sa-duties`

-- Northwest Territories income assistance -- the applicant's and recipient's questions. Every question calls the rules in
-- nt-sa.l4 and nt-sa-duties.l4; nothing is restated here. Plain inputs, one per fact the person can state. Amounts are
-- Canadian dollars a month unless the input says a year. Determinations left to the Director or an Officer (a disability,
-- an inadequate surplus, the shelter costs approved) are asked as facts.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Which program do I apply under`

@export Can I apply under the Income Assistance for Seniors and Persons with Disabilities Regulations (s 4(a))?
GIVEN `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years
      `the Director has found I have a disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Director of Income Assistance has determined that you have a disability (a permanent, persistent or prolonged impairment that significantly restricts daily living and meeting basic financial needs for 12 months or more)
      `I am the spouse of a senior or person with a disability and live with them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the spouse or common-law partner of a person 60 or over or with a disability determined by the Director, and you live with them (or the Director recognises you as their spouse)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I apply under the seniors and disabilities program` IF
    `falls within SPD s 4(a)` `my age` `the Director has found I have a disability` `I am the spouse of a senior or person with a disability and live with them`

§ `Income Assistance (the general program)`

@export Am I eligible for Income Assistance under ss 3 and 3.1 of the Income Assistance Regulations?
GIVEN `my status in Canada` IS A `Status in Canada` @desc Your status: a Canadian citizen; a permanent resident; a protected person who has applied for permanent residence and has a social insurance number; a refugee claimant whose referred claim is still open; a foreign national with a pending section 25(1) (humanitarian) request; or none of these
      `I have a seniors and disabilities application waiting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have applied under the Seniors and Persons with Disabilities Regulations and that application has not yet been decided
      `I am or was on the seniors and disabilities program` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are or have been a recipient under the Seniors and Persons with Disabilities Regulations
      `that assistance ended because I was not found to have a disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that assistance was terminated because you were not a person with a disability, or not the spouse of one
      `I am serving a sanction period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are in a one- or two-month period of ineligibility for a false statement or for failing to report a change, under either set of regulations
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I eligible for Income Assistance` IF
    `is eligible under IA ss 3 and 3.1` `my status in Canada` `I have a seniors and disabilities application waiting` `I am or was on the seniors and disabilities program` `that assistance ended because I was not found to have a disability` `I am serving a sanction period`

@export What is my family's monthly income for Income Assistance under s 22 of the Income Assistance Regulations?
GIVEN `my earned income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your earned income for the reporting period (wages including voluntary deductions, net self-employment, hunting, trapping and fishing income, honoraria, employment insurance, workers' compensation for lost income)
      `my spouse's earned income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your spouse's earned income for the reporting period, if your spouse lives with you; 0 otherwise
      `our unearned income` IS A NUMBER @desc You and your spouse's unearned income for the period (pensions, other government benefits, the GST credit, tax refunds, gifts, loans, scholarships, winnings and the like), leaving out the items s 22(6) excludes (the Canada Child Benefit, NWT Child Benefit, cost of living offset, RDSP money, treaty and land-claim money, residential school compensation and the rest)
      `of which housing benefit, student aid or labour development money` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of that unearned income is from the Canada-NWT Housing Benefit, student financial assistance or a labour development program (no $350 allowance applies to it)
      `money we hold in banks` IS A NUMBER @desc The money you and your spouse hold in banks or other financial institutions (leave out money traceable to excluded items, money in trust for a child, RESPs and approved savings plans)
      `other assets that count` IS A NUMBER @desc The value of other assets that can be turned into cash within 90 days at a loss of no more than 25% and are not exempt (your home, business assets, a vehicle, harvesting equipment and household goods are generally exempt)
      `my family's monthly budget` IS A NUMBER @desc Your family's monthly budget under the Schedule (see the budget question), used for the bank-money exemption of twice one month's needs
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my monthly income for Income Assistance` MEANS
    `the monthly income under IA s 22(1)` `my earned income` `my spouse's earned income`
        (`our unearned income` PLUS `the bank money counted under s 22(5)(r)` `money we hold in banks` `my family's monthly budget` PLUS `other assets that count`)
        `of which housing benefit, student aid or labour development money`

@export What is the most base assistance (basic benefit, or room and board) I can get each month under the Income Assistance Regulations Schedule?
GIVEN `my community` IS A `Community` @desc The community where you live (with its surrounding area)
      `basic benefit or room and board` IS A `Base assistance` @desc Whether you would get the basic benefit or, if you board, the room and board benefit
      `adults in my family` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of adults (19 or over) in your family (you, your spouse and any mature dependant)
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`What is the most Income Assistance base assistance` MEANS
    `the most IA base assistance` `my community` `basic benefit or room and board` `adults in my family`

@export What is my family's monthly budget (the cost of the benefits it needs) under the Income Assistance Regulations Schedule?
GIVEN `my community` IS A `Community` @desc The community where you live
      `basic benefit or room and board` IS A `Base assistance` @desc The basic benefit, or the room and board benefit if you board
      `adults in my family` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of adults (19 or over) in your family
      `my monthly rent` IS A NUMBER @desc Your actual monthly rent (0 if you board or own your home)
      `I live in subsidised housing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a rent subsidy is normally available for your unit (for example public housing)
      `the minimum rental rate for my unit` IS A NUMBER @desc If subsidised, the minimum rental rate for your unit; 0 otherwise
      `my monthly fuel cost` IS A NUMBER @desc The actual monthly cost of fuel you need for heating and cooking
      `my monthly utilities cost` IS A NUMBER @desc The actual monthly cost of power, water and sewage services
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`What is my Income Assistance budget` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the most IA base assistance` `my community` `basic benefit or room and board` `adults in my family`
    WHEN `answered` b THEN `answered` (b PLUS `the most rental accommodation allowance` `my monthly rent` `I live in subsidised housing` `the minimum rental rate for my unit` PLUS `my monthly fuel cost` PLUS `my monthly utilities cost`)
    WHEN `not covered` r THEN `not covered` r

@export How much Income Assistance can I get a month (the budget deficit)?
GIVEN `my family's monthly budget` IS A NUMBER @desc Your family's monthly budget (see the budget question)
      `my monthly income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your family's monthly income under s 22 (see the income question)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much Income Assistance can I get` MEANS `the budget deficit` `my family's monthly budget` `my monthly income`

@export Am I a person in need for Income Assistance under s 2 of the Income Assistance Regulations?
GIVEN `I cannot provide for my family` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you cannot provide adequately for your family because you cannot find work, lost the main provider, are ill or disabled, or for another reason
      `my budget deficit` IS A NUMBER @desc Your budget deficit (see the question on how much you can get)
      `the Director finds my surplus inadequate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you have a surplus, whether the Director has found it inadequate to provide for an unexpected situation
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years
      `I am in custody` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are incarcerated
      `I have the means to support my family` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have the means available to maintain your family adequately
      `I am not using resources open to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you refuse or neglect to use financial resources open to you, such as employment insurance
      `I am not drawing a pension open to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you refuse or neglect to draw a pension you could get (this counts only from age 65)
      `I am on the seniors and disabilities program` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a recipient under the Seniors and Persons with Disabilities Regulations
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a person in need for Income Assistance` IF
    `is a person in need under IA s 2` `I cannot provide for my family` `my budget deficit` `the Director finds my surplus inadequate` `my age` `I am in custody` `I have the means to support my family` `I am not using resources open to me` `I am not drawing a pension open to me` `I am on the seniors and disabilities program`

@export For how many months am I ineligible after a false statement, or after my assistance was ended for not reporting a change (IA ss 4, 5; SPD ss 5, 6)?
GIVEN `it happened before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were found ineligible for the same reason before
      `months since the last time` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months have passed since the last time
      `I got assistance in the last 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you received assistance in the 12 months before this finding
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How many months am I ineligible` MEANS
    `the months of ineligibility` `it happened before` `months since the last time` `I got assistance in the last 12 months`

§ `Income Assistance for Seniors and Persons with Disabilities`

@export Am I eligible under ss 4 and 4.1 of the Income Assistance for Seniors and Persons with Disabilities Regulations?
GIVEN `I can apply under the program` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are 60 or over, have a disability determined by the Director, or are the spouse of such a person (see the first question)
      `my status in Canada` IS A `Status in Canada` @desc Your status in Canada (citizen, permanent resident, protected person, refugee claimant, foreign national with a pending humanitarian request, or none of these)
      `I have an Income Assistance application waiting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have applied under the (general) Income Assistance Regulations and it has not yet been decided
      `an Officer refused me under the general regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an Officer refused you assistance under s 12(2) or s 14 of the Income Assistance Regulations
      `I am serving a sanction period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are in a one- or two-month period of ineligibility under either set of regulations
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I eligible for the seniors and disabilities program` IF
    `is eligible under SPD ss 4 and 4.1` `I can apply under the program` `my status in Canada` `I have an Income Assistance application waiting` `an Officer refused me under the general regulations` `I am serving a sanction period`

@export What is my net annual income under s 22 of the Income Assistance for Seniors and Persons with Disabilities Regulations?
GIVEN `my line 23600` IS A NUMBER @desc Your net income on line 23600 of your notice of assessment for the relevant year, in dollars a year
      `my spouse applies with me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your spouse lives with you (or is recognised by the Director) and so is part of the application
      `my spouse's line 23600` IS A NUMBER @desc Your spouse's line 23600 net income, in dollars a year; 0 if none
      `NWT social assistance we received` IS A NUMBER @desc Social assistance paid to you and your spouse by the Government of the Northwest Territories in that year, in dollars a year
      `CPP disability benefits we received` IS A NUMBER @desc Canada Pension Plan disability benefits paid to you and your spouse in that year, in dollars a year
      `other money the Director counts` IS A NUMBER @desc Any other money the Director considers to be annual income, in dollars a year; 0 if none
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my net annual income for the seniors and disabilities program` MEANS
    `the net annual income under SPD s 22(1)` `my line 23600` `my spouse applies with me` `my spouse's line 23600` `NWT social assistance we received` `CPP disability benefits we received` `other money the Director counts`

@export What is the most base assistance I can get each month under the Seniors and Persons with Disabilities Regulations Schedule?
GIVEN `my community` IS A `Community` @desc The community where you live
      `basic benefit or room and board` IS A `Base assistance` @desc The basic benefit, or the room and board benefit if you board
      `adults and seniors in my family` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of adults (19 or over) and seniors (60 or over) in your family
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`What is the most seniors and disabilities base assistance` MEANS
    `the most SPD base assistance` `my community` `basic benefit or room and board` `adults and seniors in my family`

@export What is my family's monthly budget under the Seniors and Persons with Disabilities Regulations Schedule?
GIVEN `my community` IS A `Community` @desc The community where you live
      `basic benefit or room and board` IS A `Base assistance` @desc The basic benefit, or the room and board benefit if you board
      `adults and seniors in my family` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of adults and seniors in your family
      `my monthly rent` IS A NUMBER @desc Your actual monthly rent (0 if you board or own your home)
      `I live in subsidised housing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a rent subsidy is normally available for your unit
      `the minimum rental rate for my unit` IS A NUMBER @desc If subsidised, the minimum rental rate for your unit; 0 otherwise
      `my monthly fuel cost` IS A NUMBER @desc The actual monthly cost of fuel for heating and cooking
      `my monthly utilities cost` IS A NUMBER @desc The actual monthly cost of power, water and sewage services
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`What is my seniors and disabilities budget` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the most SPD base assistance` `my community` `basic benefit or room and board` `adults and seniors in my family`
    WHEN `answered` b THEN `answered` (b PLUS `the most rental accommodation allowance` `my monthly rent` `I live in subsidised housing` `the minimum rental rate for my unit` PLUS `my monthly fuel cost` PLUS `my monthly utilities cost`)
    WHEN `not covered` r THEN `not covered` r

@export How much assistance can I get a month under the Seniors and Persons with Disabilities Regulations?
GIVEN `my family's monthly budget` IS A NUMBER @desc Your family's monthly budget under the Schedule (see the budget question)
      `my net annual income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your net annual income under s 22 (see the income question), in dollars a year
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much seniors and disabilities assistance can I get` MEANS
    `the SPD monthly budget deficit` `my family's monthly budget` `my net annual income`

@export Am I a person in need under s 3 of the Income Assistance for Seniors and Persons with Disabilities Regulations?
GIVEN `my budget deficit` IS A NUMBER @desc Your monthly budget deficit (see the question on how much you can get)
      `the Director finds my surplus inadequate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you have a surplus, whether the Director has found it inadequate for an unexpected situation
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years
      `I am in custody` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are incarcerated
      `I have the means to support my family` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have the means available to maintain your family adequately
      `I am not using resources open to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you refuse or neglect to use financial resources open to you, such as employment
      `I am not drawing a pension open to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you refuse or neglect to draw a pension you could get (you need not draw one before 65)
      `my family's money in banks` IS A NUMBER @desc The total money held in banks or other financial institutions by you and every member of your family, in dollars
      `I am on the general Income Assistance program` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a recipient under the (general) Income Assistance Regulations
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a person in need for the seniors and disabilities program` IF
    `is a person in need under SPD s 3` `my budget deficit` `the Director finds my surplus inadequate` `my age` `I am in custody` `I have the means to support my family` `I am not using resources open to me` `I am not drawing a pension open to me` `my family's money in banks` `I am on the general Income Assistance program`

§ `Reporting and deadlines`

@export By what date must I report a change in my circumstances (s 19(1) of either regulation)?
GIVEN `my program` IS A `Stream` @desc Which regulations you receive assistance under: the Income Assistance Regulations, or the Seniors and Persons with Disabilities Regulations
      `the day of the change` IS A DATE @desc The date your circumstances changed (family members, income, assets, residence or anything else that may affect your assistance)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I report a change` MEANS `the last day to report a change` `my program` `the day of the change`

@export If I had no proof of my social insurance number when I applied, by what date must I prove I have applied for one (IA s 10(3), SPD s 11(5))?
GIVEN `the date I applied` IS A DATE @desc The date of your application for assistance
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I prove my social insurance number application` MEANS
    `the last day to prove a social insurance number application` `the date I applied`

@export By what date must I provide the information and documents for a seniors and disabilities application (SPD s 11(3))?
GIVEN `the date I applied` IS A DATE @desc The date of your application
      `extra days the Officer allowed` IS A NUMBER @desc If the Officer allowed more time within the eligibility period, the total number of days allowed from the date of application; 0 if not
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I provide my seniors and disabilities documents` MEANS
    `the last day to provide the SPD s 11(2) documents` `the date I applied` `extra days the Officer allowed`

§ `Appeals`

@export Can I appeal this decision under s 8 of the Social Assistance Act?
GIVEN `I applied for or receive assistance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an applicant for or recipient of assistance
      `the decision` IS A `Decision` @desc What the Officer's or Director's decision was about: your eligibility, the amount of your assistance, or something else
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I appeal` IF `may appeal under Act s 8(1)` `I applied for or receive assistance` `the decision`
